/// the colour of the words beside them, as Discord draws a store button and a
/// game's links (Alex, 2026-11-18: "replace all the play icons with discord's
/// icons").
///
/// **Not `BrandMark`'s tiles.** Those are a brand's mark on the brand's own
/// colour, for a person's connected accounts. A store button and a game's
/// links are where Discord draws the bare mark in the text's colour.
///
/// **Converted, not traced**: the 24-unit paths of Discord's icons, read off its
/// bundle on 2026-11-18, with every arc and quadratic resolved to a cubic
/// (`VectorPath` reads M/L/C/Z only). Each part keeps its own fill rule: Steam,
/// Instagram, Reddit and the globe cut their holes even-odd in some parts and
/// not in others.
